From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: Scale the audio backpressure duration only

Do not scale the absolute monotonic clock origin when applying playback
speed to the existing backpressure allowance. Scaling the absolute
deadline makes slow playback expire immediately at sufficient uptime
and fast playback wait far beyond the intended duration. Keep sample
ownership, credit handling and timeout constants unchanged.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/AudioSinkAE.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/AudioSinkAE.cpp
@@ -116,8 +116,9 @@
   double timeout;
   timeout  = DVD_SEC_TO_TIME(m_pAudioStream->GetDelay()) + audioframe.duration;
   timeout += DVD_SEC_TO_TIME(1.0);
+  // Scale the duration, not the absolute clock origin.
+  timeout *= m_pClock->GetClockSpeed();
   timeout += m_pClock->GetAbsoluteClock();
-  timeout *= m_pClock->GetClockSpeed();
 
   unsigned int total = audioframe.nb_frames - audioframe.framesOut;
   unsigned int frames = total;
